/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1492,"endPos":1640,"startLine":39,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":41,"endLineOffset":5,"length":149}]},{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java-server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java--1646:1968","promptId":"#6C9E4","srcPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java","dstPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1646,"endPos":1968,"startLine":43,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":5,"length":323}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":48,"line":49,"comment_lines":["[][49]"],"review_comment":["If you use the cranky breaker service it\u0027ll blow up *randomly* and you can assert that you always freed the memory, no matter the random explosion. I rather like it for this sort of thing.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhich one of your tests hits a the breaker exception you are guarding?\r\n","\u003e Which one of your tests hits a the breaker exception you are guarding?\r\n\r\nThe `testReadWithData()`. The reserve is only called when it has data in it. So I added that one explicitly.\r\n\r\nAbout the cranky breaker, I\u0027m not sure we want it to break randomly. This has multiple potential breaking points I wanted to test (Add memory and release on error, on every constructor).\r\n\r\nThe cranky breaks 1/20 times. If we\u0027re fine with this one (The full suite takes around 1 second on my machine), I would leave it as-is. It tests every potential breaking point (_Divided in 16 random seeds_).\r\nIs it too much? Not sure","\u003eAbout the cranky breaker, I\u0027m not sure we want it to break randomly. This has multiple potential breaking points I wanted to test (Add memory and release on error, on every constructor).\r\n\r\nThat\u0027s where the cranky is really good at.","Just updated it to use the cranky breaker. It will fail ~1/5 times, so I guess it\u0027s ok. I suppose even 1/20 times would be ok for something like this.\r\nI guess I was reinventing the wheel here XD"],"path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java","id":37814,"created_at":"2024-10-10T13:40:50Z","original_position":27,"side":"RIGHT","position":28,"submitted_on_commit":"b3afc14824b2494dc26f4a7b7fe9967058d04c61","diff_hunk":"@@ -32,14 +36,75 @@ public TDigestStateReleasingTests(TDigestState.Type digestType) {\n         this.digestType \u003d digestType;\n     }\n \n+    public void testCreateOfType() {\n+        testCircuitBreakerTrip(circuitBreaker -\u003e TDigestState.createOfType(circuitBreaker, digestType, 100));\n+    }\n+\n+    public void testCreateUsingParamsFrom() {\n+        testCircuitBreakerTrip(circuitBreaker -\u003e {\n+            try (TDigestState example \u003d TDigestState.createOfType(newLimitedBreaker(ByteSizeValue.ofMb(100)), digestType, 100)) {\n+                return TDigestState.createUsingParamsFrom(example);\n+            }\n+        });","submitted_line":48},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"In the `read` method, the exception handling now includes a call to `Releasables.close(state)`. Ensure that `TDigestState` implements `Closeable` or has a proper `close` method. If not, this will cause a compilation error. Additionally, ensure that `createUsingParamsFrom` is defined in the `TDigestState` class or imported from another class.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestState.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestState.java-9254:9276,9285:9351,9360:9455,9464:9477-9260:9630","promptId":"#DQ92A","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/